  },
  {
    "@id": "ArtifactNode/00C7BJX360000",
    "@type": "ArtifactNode",
    "artifactId": "00C7BJX360000",
    "fileHash": "17fc83bc70d013c020b5e1e69c979a124ed99b457caf5f710dcb7bbae9ddda0c",
    "lastTrackedAt": "2026-08-31T23:02:27.480Z",
    "path": "Aperas-artifact-projection-design.md",
    "title": "Aperas-artifact-projection-design.md",
    "ingestedHash": "17fc83bc70d013c020b5e1e69c979a124ed99b457caf5f710dcb7bbae9ddda0c",
    "lastIngestedAt": "2026-08-31T23:02:36.096Z",
    "root": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ6G0000",
    "text": "`Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A names three projection modes that turn a stored\n`BlockNode` tree back into an output: Artifact Projection (serialize back to the physical\n`.md` file, always fully unfolded regardless of each block's `unfolded` state), the Human UI,\nand the Agentic BFS interface. This doc settles the design for the first of the three —\nArtifact Projection, the direct inverse of `astParser.ts`'s Markdown → tree transform. The\nother two modes are out of scope here. The design below is settled; nothing has been\nimplemented yet."
  },
  {
    "@id": "ArtifactNode/00C7BJX3S0000",
    "@type": "ArtifactNode",
    "artifactId": "00C7BJX3S0000",
    "fileHash": "20332acc4c9cec651d11785a2c8018a5ccef052aec86f41461696297d5718be7",
    "lastTrackedAt": "2026-08-31T23:02:27.556Z",
    "path": "Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md",
    "title": "Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md",
    "ingestedHash": "20332acc4c9cec651d11785a2c8018a5ccef052aec86f41461696297d5718be7",
    "lastIngestedAt": "2026-08-31T23:02:36.251Z",
    "root": "BlockNode/00C7BJZ7PR000",
    "text": "The original roadmap (`Aperas-design.md`'s Development Roadmap) only ever named one assertion-\nrelated deliverable — Phase 2's \"graph search skill\" — and treated the Human UI (Phase 1) as\nthe thing that lets humans/agents see what's in the graph at all. Neither assumption survived\nPhase 0 finishing:"
  },
  {
    "@id": "ArtifactNode/00C7BJX5YR000",
    "@type": "ArtifactNode",
    "artifactId": "00C7BJX5YR000",
    "fileHash": "c22bb7eed0caa32b0a27f250add71b4df1a873a7d609dd0f7ec6d133f22fe5c7",
    "lastTrackedAt": "2026-08-31T23:02:27.835Z",
    "path": "Aperas-extensibility.md",
    "title": "Aperas-extensibility.md",
    "ingestedHash": "c22bb7eed0caa32b0a27f250add71b4df1a873a7d609dd0f7ec6d133f22fe5c7",
    "lastIngestedAt": "2026-08-31T23:02:37.732Z",
    "root": "BlockNode/00C7BJZK8R000",
    "text": "Aperas is not a monolithic application with a single, closed database; it is an engine for growing forms (Perata) out of a formless core (Apeiron)."
  },
  {
    "@id": "ArtifactNode/00C7BJX6JG000",
    "@type": "ArtifactNode",
    "artifactId": "00C7BJX6JG000",
    "fileHash": "dbc83bd670b3b4ead48e76b4620cbcfec31f3a0b89d2dc98b092c94ebf31b88c",
    "lastTrackedAt": "2026-08-31T23:02:27.914Z",
    "path": "Aperas-fractal-ontology-implementation-plan.md",
    "title": "Aperas-fractal-ontology-implementation-plan.md",
    "ingestedHash": "dbc83bd670b3b4ead48e76b4620cbcfec31f3a0b89d2dc98b092c94ebf31b88c",
    "lastIngestedAt": "2026-08-31T23:02:37.864Z",
    "root": "BlockNode/00C7BJZMA0000",
    "text": "This plan outlines the steps to refactor the Aperas Knowledge Graph codebase to implement the fractal block-tree ontology designed in `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md`. Stage 1 is fully implemented and live-verified; Stage 2 is implemented except items 4 (Link Extraction) and 5 (Title vs. Text Split), which remain open; Stage 3 (Database & UI Alignment) hasn't started. See `Aperas-dev-status.md` for current status and `Aperas-architecture.md` for the as-built reference. Node identity evolved past what Stage 2 anticipated (content-addressed hashing was tried and superseded by Snowflake-style ids — see `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` Appendix F); this plan is kept as a historical record, not a live checklist."
  },
  {
    "@id": "ArtifactNode/00C7BJX82G000",
    "@type": "ArtifactNode",
    "artifactId": "00C7BJX82G000",
    "fileHash": "7f58c31f776c5849148140280409161e518e569760a197b8d58ea29a2dfd1177",
    "lastTrackedAt": "2026-08-31T23:02:28.106Z",
    "path": "Aperas-interactive-summarization-design.md",
    "title": "Aperas-interactive-summarization-design.md",
    "ingestedHash": "7f58c31f776c5849148140280409161e518e569760a197b8d58ea29a2dfd1177",
    "lastIngestedAt": "2026-08-31T23:02:38.030Z",
    "root": "BlockNode/00C7BJZNKG000",
    "text": "**Implemented and live-verified.** `kg:title`/`kg:link` (`kgCli.ts`), `updateBlockNode` (`crud.ts`\n§2), and the `reconcileNode`/`resolveBlockLinks` persistence fix (§4/§7) are all live against the\nreal `aperas` DB — a title and a cross-link set via these commands both survived a real\nre-ingestion round-trip (confirmed via direct `doc get`, not just the tools' own success output).\nOne implementation-time bug found and fixed beyond what this doc anticipated: `rl.question()`\n(readline/promises) races against stream-end when real `await`s happen between prompts — piped,\nnon-interactive stdin (the coding-agent-driving-the-tool case this doc is built around) hit both\nan immediate throw and a silently-abandoned hung call depending on timing. Fixed by consuming the\nreadline interface's own async iterator instead of `.question()` — see `createLineReader` in\n`kgCli.ts`. Also found live: `graphql.ts`'s block field selection never included `links` at all,\nso `oldNode.links` was always `undefined` regardless of the `reconcileNode` fix — added `links {\n_id }` to `blockFieldSelection` plus a `normalizeLinks` step (mirroring the existing\n`normalizeProps`/`_json` pattern) to convert GraphQL's full-IRI `_id` down to the short ref-id\nstring form `updateDocument` expects."
  },
  {
    "@id": "ArtifactNode/00C7BJX8MR000",
    "@type": "ArtifactNode",
    "artifactId": "00C7BJX8MR000",
    "fileHash": "ab9b417e7892f7b797858c73ed913a71f910a84ba29cfdd72572c64d6a549763",
    "lastTrackedAt": "2026-08-31T23:02:28.179Z",
    "path": "Aperas-markdown-fractal-mapping-design.md",
    "title": "Aperas-markdown-fractal-mapping-design.md",
    "ingestedHash": "ab9b417e7892f7b797858c73ed913a71f910a84ba29cfdd72572c64d6a549763",
    "lastIngestedAt": "2026-08-31T23:02:38.215Z",
    "root": "BlockNode/00C7BJZQ1G000",
    "text": "Markdown/mdast is a **loose** structure: node shapes vary per type (a `heading` carries its\ncontent differently from a `paragraph`; `list`/`listItem` nest oddly; whole categories of block\nexist that the parser doesn't even recognize without extra plugins), and remark itself parses\nheadings as flat siblings rather than a nesting construct. `BlockNode` is meant to be a **tight**,\nuniform structure with no fixed depth bound — the same three-part shape at every depth, described\nby `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5's \"Abstraction by Folding\": *\"an unbounded subtree folds\ninto an abstract (`text`), which folds into a semantic label (`title`), which folds into a hidden\n`@id`.\"* That's a claim of **uniformity** — every node, regardless of its mdast origin, is\nsupposed to look the same shape-wise. In practice, the mapping in `astParser.ts` has grown\nad hoc, one exception at a time (heading gets special title handling, containers get emptied\ntext, `ordered`/`start`/`checked` bolted on for `list`/`listItem` specifically). This doc is the\nsettled mapping: what `title`/`text`/`children` mean for every block type, uniformly, and an\nhonest audit of what's covered today versus silently isn't."
  },
  {
    "@id": "ArtifactNode/00C7BJX980000",
    "@type": "ArtifactNode",
    "artifactId": "00C7BJX980000",
    "fileHash": "23b17a1b312116c0199c9dba66f0b829d586facf5ff99244ad01545362af6c3f",
    "lastTrackedAt": "2026-08-31T23:02:28.256Z",
    "path": "Aperas-reconciliation-matching-design.md",
    "title": "Aperas-reconciliation-matching-design.md",
    "ingestedHash": "23b17a1b312116c0199c9dba66f0b829d586facf5ff99244ad01545362af6c3f",
    "lastIngestedAt": "2026-08-31T23:02:38.453Z",
    "root": "BlockNode/00C7BJZRX8000",
    "text": "Re-ingesting an already-ingested artifact today just orphans its entire prior `BlockNode` tree. The strategy for doing better was settled in `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1.B and Appendix F; this doc works out the algorithm that actually does it. The design below is settled; nothing has been implemented yet."
  },
  {
    "@id": "ArtifactNode/00C7BJXATR000",
    "@type": "ArtifactNode",
    "artifactId": "00C7BJXATR000",
    "fileHash": "9a30d15ed0087d53647f53c919f6b8af22086568c1bc1a2ebcd4b598d19118a3",
    "lastTrackedAt": "2026-08-31T23:02:28.459Z",
    "path": "tdb-cli-status-walkthrough.md",
    "title": "tdb-cli-status-walkthrough.md",
    "ingestedHash": "9a30d15ed0087d53647f53c919f6b8af22086568c1bc1a2ebcd4b598d19118a3",
    "lastIngestedAt": "2026-08-31T23:02:38.598Z",
    "root": "BlockNode/00C7BJZT1G000",
    "text": "Operational reference for checking status, commit logs, document contents, and remote state of the `aperas` database using the `tdb` CLI shortcut. For complete reference of TerminusDB CLI, see the [official documentation](https://terminusdb.org/docs/terminusdb-cli-commands/)."
  },
  {
    "@id": "ArtifactNode/00C7BJXCC8000",
    "@type": "ArtifactNode",
    "artifactId": "00C7BJXCC8000",
    "fileHash": "8e838f426d480acd4f8c5f2e72c161a850c37f8ed1d0fed88bfab2418b87e9b8",
    "lastTrackedAt": "2026-08-31T23:02:28.657Z",
    "path": "terminusdb-issue-bundle-cross-store.md",
    "title": "terminusdb-issue-bundle-cross-store.md",
    "ingestedHash": "8e838f426d480acd4f8c5f2e72c161a850c37f8ed1d0fed88bfab2418b87e9b8",
